# busybox -- the userland the initramfs runs before the real root exists.
#
# The initramfs cannot use the system's own tools. Everything in Duct is
# dynamically linked against /usr/lib, and at the point /init runs there is no
# /usr: the root filesystem is still inside a squashfs on a device nobody has
# found yet. Carrying glibc, the dynamic loader, mount, blkid, losetup and a
# shell into the initramfs and getting every library path right is possible;
# one 1 MB static binary that is all of those is simply better.
#
# It is also why this package is not a general-purpose userland. Only
# /usr/bin/busybox is installed -- no applet symlinks -- so it cannot collide
# with uutils-coreutils or util-linux over /usr/bin/ls or /usr/bin/mount. The
# initramfs makes its own symlinks, where nothing else has an opinion.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env. The
# sha256 matches the one busybox.net publishes next to the tarball.
SRC_URL=https://busybox.net/downloads/busybox-1.37.0.tar.bz2
SRC_SHA256=3311dff32e746499f4df0d5df04d7eb396382d7e108bb9250e7b519b837043a4
SRC_DIR=busybox-1.37.0
